Ablation panel ("Ours") for Ultralytics trackers, used by every BoT-SORT result of the paper.

Base: ultralytics 8.4.84 == git commit cc8576c36f881e474a034ba5e1a534f89720bbf0 (the five patched files are
identical in the PyPI wheel and in that commit). Files: trackers/bot_sort.py, trackers/byte_tracker.py,
trackers/utils/kalman_filter.py, trackers/utils/matching.py, cfg/trackers/botsort.yaml.

Adds: omega occlusion signal, ReID firewall, DIoU rescue, omega innovation penalty (all gated, off by default),
static-object velocity prior (static_prior_beta) and a w/h floor (min_wh_clamp). The paper's BoT-SORT uses
static_prior_beta=0.2 and min_wh_clamp=5.0 (configs/trackers/botsort.yaml). New dependency: scipy.
KalmanFilterXYWH.update uses a Cholesky solve (scipy) instead of np.linalg.solve.

Apply to an installed package:   patch -p1 -d "$(python -c 'import ultralytics, os; print(os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(ultralytics.__file__)))')" < patches/ultralytics_ours.patch
Apply to a source checkout:      git apply patches/ultralytics_ours.patch
